  "derivation_method": [
    "Validate all eight saved RPC captures with the existing collector offline validators: request parameters, endpoint, JSON-RPC IDs, block identities, checksums, lengths and response membership.",
    "Reconstruct each result-42 validator_account_audit independently from flattened dotted keys, using row_kind boundaries. Do not join independent repeated arrays by flattened row position.",
    "Filter RPC records by validator_accounts_update cause; compare distinct account-ID sets and update-record counts separately. Retain response-array indices and within-account cause order.",
    "Parse monetary strings as Decimal and use integer/Fraction arithmetic to reconstruct nearest binary64 values from saved FLOAT decimal text; compare exact integer-yoctoNEAR RPC states with those values and with saved BIGNUMERIC-derived combined balances. Never pass monetary values through float.",
    "Use a conservative two-ULP observational comparison screen, while reporting failures of direct nearest-binary64 equality. The screen is not an established ingestion error bound or a measure of source accuracy.",
    "Assign account shard IDs from the saved V3 sorted boundary_accounts and shard_ids with bisect_right; compare header height_included with the target height to identify shards without a new chunk.",
    "Compare sorted per-shard RPC validator-account rank with saved blank-chunk indices. RPC does not expose shard IDs or source index_in_block, so these ranks are inferred rather than returned ordering metadata.",
    "Count candidate index collisions and omitted validator observations. Preserve unavailable before-states, monetary changes, independently measured issuance and actual burn as null."
  ],
